 ",{"id":203,"html":204},"handnote","\u003Cp>Large v-cut letters with standard serifs; P is slightly open, B has smaller upper loop (both closed). Deep triangular interpuncts.\u003C/p> Line 1  69-72  Interlineation line 1 to 2    ",{"id":206,"html":207},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[209,211,214,215],{"html":210},"Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy Prag 2015-01-16, cassette 16, magazzino B, Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi",{"id":212,"lang":131,"html":213},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"o · Cai · filio · Poblilia tribu\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"o\">\u003Cspan data-text=\"o\">ọ\u003C/span>\u003C/span> · \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Cai\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Cai\">C(ai)\u003C/span>\u003C/span> · f(ilio) · Pob(lilia) (\u003Cem>scil.\u003C/em> tribu)\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":210},{"id":216,"lang":131,"html":217},"edition-diplomatic","\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"o · Cai · filio · Poblilia tribu\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"o\">\u003Cspan data-text=\"o\">.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>·\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Cai\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Cai\">C\u003C/span>\u003C/span>·F·POB(\u003Cem>scil.\u003C/em> TRIBU)\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",[219,221,224,226],{"image":105,"thumb":220,"title":108},"ISic001788_tiled-thumb.tif",{"image":222,"thumb":223,"title":108},"ISic001788.jpg","ISic001788-thumb.jpg",{"image":111,"thumb":225,"title":108},"ISic001788_rear_tiled-thumb.tif",{"image":227,"thumb":228,"title":108},"ISic001788_rear.jpg","ISic001788_rear-thumb.jpg",[230],{"html":58},"\u003C?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"https://epidoc.stoa.org/schema/latest/tei-epidoc.rng\" type=\"application/xml\" schematypens=\"http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"../schematron/ircyr-checking.sch\" schematypens=\"http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron\"?>\n\u003CTEI xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:xi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude\" xml:lang=\"en\">\n    \u003CteiHeader>\n        \u003CfileDesc>\n            \u003CtitleStmt>\n                \u003Ctitle>Fragment of a Latin inscription\u003C/title>\n                \u003Ceditor ref=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/editor>\n                \u003Cprincipal ref=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/principal>\n                \u003Cfunder>John Fell OUP Research Fund\u003C/funder>\n\t   \u003Cfunder>\u003Cref target=\"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/885040\">ERC Advanced Grant no.885040\u003C/ref>\u003C/funder>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"JP\" ref=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>original data collection and editing\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n               \u003C/titleStmt>\n            \u003CpublicationStmt>\n                \u003Cauthority>I.Sicily\u003C/authority>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"filename\">ISic001788\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"TM\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDR\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDH\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDCS\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"PHI\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"URI\">http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001788\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cavailability>\n                    \u003Clicence target=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.\u003C/licence>\n                \u003C/availability>\n            \u003C/publicationStmt>\n            \u003CsourceDesc>\n                \u003CmsDesc>\n                    \u003CmsIdentifier>\n                        \u003Ccountry>Italy\u003C/country>\n                        \u003Cregion>Sicily\u003C/region>\n                        \u003Crepository role=\"museum\" ref=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/097\">Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi\u003C/repository>\n                        \u003Cidno type=\"inventory\"/>\n                        \u003CaltIdentifier>\n                            \u003Csettlement/>\n                            \u003Crepository/>\n                            \u003Cidno type=\"old\"/>\n                        \u003C/altIdentifier>\n                    \u003C/msIdentifier>\n                    \u003CmsContents>\n                        \u003CtextLang mainLang=\"la\">Latin\u003C/textLang>\n                    \u003C/msContents>\n                    \u003CphysDesc>\n                        \u003CobjectDesc>\n                            \u003CsupportDesc>\n                                \u003Csupport>\u003Cp>Two joining fragments of a fine pale grey marble plaque, previously glued together but now separated. The reverse is finished smooth, and shows marks around the edge which imply it was stuck to a wall at some previous point in this form (for display?). The right hand fragment preserves part of the upper margin, but otherwise the fragments are broken on all sides. (frag. a (left) is H. 17.6 x W 14.5 cm; frag. b (right) is H 20.3 x W 12.9 cm).\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble\" type=\"stone.marble\" subtype=\"unverified\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html\">marble\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.plaque\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259\">plaque\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">20.3\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\">26.7\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\">2.1 (left) to 1.9 (right)\u003C/depth>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.fragments.contiguous\"/>\n\t\t    \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\u003Cp>There is a large vacat (11.5 cm to the upper margin) above the single preserved line of letters, implying this is the first line of the text.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.chiselled\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1\">chiselled\u003C/rs>\n                                \t\u003Cdamage ana=\"#text_condition.incomplete\"/>\n\t\t\t\u003C/layout>\n                            \u003C/layoutDesc>\n                        \u003C/objectDesc>\n                        \u003ChandDesc>\n                            \u003ChandNote>\u003Cp>Large v-cut letters with standard serifs; P is slightly open, B has smaller upper loop (both closed). Deep triangular interpuncts.\u003C/p>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line1\">Line 1\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"69\" atMost=\"72\">69-72\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line2\">Interlineation line 1 to 2\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"interlinear\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\"/>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                            \u003C/handNote>\n                        \u003C/handDesc>\n                    \u003C/physDesc>\n                    \u003Chistory>\n                        \u003Corigin>\n                            \u003CorigPlace>\u003Cregion>Sicilia\u003C/region>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"ancient\" ref=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462503\">Syracusae\u003C/placeName>\t\t\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"modern\" ref=\"http://sws.geonames.org/2523083\">Siracusa\u003C/placeName>\n                            \t\u003Cgeo>37.08415, 15.27628\u003C/geo>\n\t\t\u003C/origPlace>\n                            \u003CorigDate datingMethod=\"#julian\" notBefore-custom=\"-0021\" notAfter-custom=\"0050\" evidence=\"lettering\">Augustan / first half of the first century CE\u003C/origDate>\n                        \u003C/origin>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"found\" subtype=\"discovered\" notAfter=\"1888\">No record of discovery is preserved, but the right hand fragment is recorded in Orsi's first notebook (Sept. 1888) among fragments already in the museum.\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"observed\" subtype=\"autopsied\" xml:id=\"autopsy\">Prag 2015-01-16, cassette 16, magazzino B, Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003Cacquisition/>\n                    \u003C/history>\n                \u003C/msDesc>\n            \u003C/sourceDesc>\n        \u003C/fileDesc>\n        \u003CencodingDesc>\n             \u003Cp>Encoded following the latest EpiDoc guidelines\u003C/p>\n             \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/ISicily-taxonomies.xml\">\n                 \u003Cxi:fallback>\n                     \u003Cp>Taxonomies for ISicily controlled values\u003C/p>\n                 \u003C/xi:fallback>\n             \u003C/xi:include>\n\t  \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/charDecl.xml\">\n\t     \u003Cxi:fallback>\n\t       \u003Cp>ISicily glyphs authority list\u003C/p>\n\t     \u003C/xi:fallback>\n\t   \u003C/xi:include>\n         \u003C/encodingDesc>\n        \u003CprofileDesc>\n            \u003CcalendarDesc>\n                \u003Ccalendar xml:id=\"julian\">\n                    \u003Cp>Julian Calendar\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/calendar>\n            \u003C/calendarDesc>\n            \u003ClangUsage>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"en\">English\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"it\">Italian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"grc\">Ancient Greek\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"la\">Latin\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"he\">Hebrew\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"phn\">Phoenician\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xpu\">Punic\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"osc\">Oscan\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xly\">Elymian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"scx\">Sikel\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"sxc\">Sikan\u003C/language>\n            \u003C/langUsage>\n            \u003CtextClass>\n                \u003Ckeywords scheme=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription\">\n                    \u003Cterm ana=\"#function.honorific\" ref=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Honorific\" cert=\"low\">honorific\u003C/term>\n                \u003C/keywords>\n            \u003C/textClass>\n        \u003C/profileDesc>\n        \u003CrevisionDesc status=\"edited\">\n            \u003ClistChange>\n                \u003Cchange when=\"2026-05-13\" who=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag created file from autopsy\u003C/change>\n\t\u003C/listChange>\n        \u003C/revisionDesc>\n    \u003C/teiHeader>\n    \u003Cfacsimile>\n        \u003Csurface type=\"front\">\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"screen\" url=\"ISic001788_tiled.tif\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2015-01-16\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"print\" url=\"ISic001788.jpg\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2015-01-16\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n         \u003C/surface>\n        \u003Csurface type=\"rear\">\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"screen\" url=\"ISic001788_rear_tiled.tif\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2015-01-16\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"print\" url=\"ISic001788_rear.jpg\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2015-01-16\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n        \u003C/surface>\n    \u003C/facsimile>\n    \u003Ctext>\n        \u003Cbody>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"edition\" subtype=\"primary\" xml:space=\"preserve\" xml:lang=\"la\" resp=\"#JP\" source=\"#autopsy\">\n                    \u003Cab>\n                         \u003Clb n=\"1\"/>\u003Cgap reason=\"lost\" extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/>\u003CpersName type=\"attested\">\u003Cname>\u003Cw part=\"F\">\u003Cunclear>o\u003C/unclear>\u003C/w>\u003C/name> \u003Cg ref=\"#interpunct\">·\u003C/g> \u003CpersName type=\"attested\">\u003Cname>\u003Cexpan>\u003Cabbr>C\u003C/abbr>\u003Cex>ai\u003C/ex>\u003C/expan>\u003C/name>\u003C/persName> \u003Cg ref=\"#interpunct\">·\u003C/g> \u003Cexpan>\u003Cabbr>f\u003C/abbr>\u003Cex>ilio\u003C/ex>\u003C/expan> \u003Cg ref=\"#interpunct\">·\u003C/g> \u003CorgName>\u003Cexpan>\u003Cabbr>Pob\u003C/abbr>\u003Cex>lilia\u003C/ex>\u003C/expan>\u003C/orgName> \u003Csupplied reason=\"subaudible\">tribu\u003C/supplied>\u003C/persName> \u003Cgap reason=\"lost\" extent=\"unknown\" unit=\"character\"/>\n                    \u003C/ab>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"apparatus\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003ClistApp>\n                    \u003Capp>\u003Cnote>Text based on autopsy\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                    \u003Capp loc=\"1\">\u003Cnote>Trace of curve on the break at the start of the line must be from an O\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                    \u003C/listApp> \n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"translation\" xml:lang=\"en\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cp>[---]o, son of Gaius, of the Poblilia tribe [---]\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"commentary\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cp>This is presumably an honorific inscription for an individual, who was named in line 1 of the text and part of whose name is here preserved. The use of the dative (the partial trace of O at the start of the fragment) indicates the likely honorific form of the text, and the partial preservation of the upper edge and the vacat above the letters indicate that this is the first line of the text. The size of the letters speaks to a monumental public text. The Poblilia tribe is only attested once in Sicily, in a Severan period honorific from Lilybaeum (\u003Cref target=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000492\">ISic000492\u003C/ref>), and in Syracusae itself only the Maecia and the Quirina (the most commonly attested tribe in Sicily) are attested (see Prag, J. R. W., ‘Sicilia Romana Tributim Discripta’, in Le Tribù Romane. Atti Della XVIe Rencontre Sur l’épigraphie (Bari 8-10 Ottobre 2009), ed. by M. Silvestrini (Edipuglia, 2010), pp. 305–11). The form of the letters suggests this text likely belongs to the Augustan / Julio-Claudian period. The text is previously unpublished, and although the right-hand fragment is recorded in Orsi's first notebook, indicating that it was present in the museum's collection prior to his arrival in 1888, there is no record of the left-hand fragment, nor of the provenance of either.\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"bibliography\">\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"edition\">\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Orsi\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>2018\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>Tacc. 1, p.72 (no.88)\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/RGRSRUHK\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002617\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002617\u003C/ref>\u003C/bibl>\n                \u003C/listBibl>\n\t   \u003ClistBibl type=\"discussion\">\u003Cbibl/>\u003C/listBibl>\n            \u003C/div>\n        \u003C/body>\n    \u003C/text>\n\u003C/TEI>\n"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
